---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { href, repoFile } from "../lib/site";

// What the app downloads, and when (docs/Third-party licenses.md, the
// features that use them, and the model ids in the source).
const MODELS = [
  { feature: "Auto captions, filler words, edit by transcript", model: "Whisper (tiny, base or small, by your choice)", size: "41 to 249 MB" },
  { feature: "Text to speech and voiceover", model: "Kokoro-82M", size: "about 90 MB" },
  { feature: "Remove background, text behind the subject", model: "ormbg on a GPU with WebGPU; MediaPipe Selfie otherwise", size: "88 MB, or 0.5 MB" },
];
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="OpenFrame is local-first: no account, no server, no telemetry. What the app connects to and why, where your work is stored, and what this website collects (nothing)."
>
  <section class="page-hero" style="--glow-a: rgb(47 210 122 / 14%); --glow-b: rgb(47 123 255 / 14%);">
    <div class="light" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Local-first. No telemetry.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        OpenFrame has no account, no server of ours and no analytics. Your footage, your projects and your exports stay on your
        computer. Here is everything the app connects to, and how we checked.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap privacy">
      <div class="copy-block">
        <h2>The app</h2>

        <h3>What it never does</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>It does not upload your media, projects or exports anywhere.</li>
          <li>It has no account, sign-in or license server.</li>
          <li>It contains no analytics, telemetry, crash reporting or advertising code.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What it connects to, and when</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Hugging Face, once per model.</strong> The AI features that need a model download it the first time you use
            them, then work offline:
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Model</th><th>Download</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {MODELS.map((m) => <tr><td>{m.feature}</td><td>{m.model}</td><td>{m.size}</td></tr>)}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>A model server on your own computer,</strong> for the AI assistant: Ollama (127.0.0.1:11434) or LM Studio
            (127.0.0.1:1234), if you run one. The desktop app reaches only those two local addresses for it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your browser, when you click a link,</strong> such as the install guide for Claude Code or Codex when the app
            cannot find them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Nothing else on its own.</strong> The desktop app's content security policy allows network connections only
            to the app itself and to Hugging Face. Manual editing and export work fully offline.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Where your work lives</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Desktop:</strong> projects are JSON files in the app's data folder, with the previous version kept as a backup. Your media stays where it is on disk; projects refer to it by path.</li>
          <li><strong>Web build:</strong> projects and imported media live in your browser's private storage for that site, on your device. Clearing site data removes them.</li>
          <li><strong>Exports</strong> go where you choose; an agent's exports go to your Videos folder.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>AI agents</h3>
        <p>
          The MCP server for agents is off until you turn on Allow AI agents. It listens only on 127.0.0.1, refuses requests
          from other websites, and needs the token made for your install. An agent that connects runs on your computer with
          your permission; what that agent sends to its own provider is between you and that provider, as with any other use
          of it. <a href={href("ai/")}>More on the safety model</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>How we checked</h3>
        <p>
          On October 18, 2026, at revision <code>757159b</code>, we searched the app's source and dependency lists for analytics,
          telemetry and crash-reporting code (there is none), listed every network address in the TypeScript and Rust source,
          read the desktop app's content security policy, and confirmed the Rust side has no HTTP client beyond its own local
          servers. This is a review of the code, not a network audit of a release; it will be repeated for the first packaged
          release, and the <a href={repoFile("docs/Release preparation.md")}>release checklist</a> tracks it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="site-box" aria-labelledby="site-title">
        <span class="mark" style="--hue: var(--green)"><Icon name="lock" size={20} /></span>
        <h2 id="site-title">This website</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No cookies, analytics, trackers or third-party scripts.</li>
          <li>No fonts, images or videos from other servers: everything is served from this site.</li>
          <li>Static pages hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub, as the host, receives the usual request information, such as your IP address, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its privacy statement</a>.</li>
          <li>The films play only when you press play.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .section-tight { padding-bottom: 40px; }
  .privacy { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 4fr); gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px); align-items: start; }
  .privacy h2 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
  .privacy .copy-block h3 { margin-top: 2em; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-card); }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; color: var(--text-2); }
  th { color: var(--text-1); font-weight: 600; background: rgb(255 255 255 / 3%); }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .site-box { position: sticky; top: 96px; padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--r-card); background: var(--bg-1); }
  .site-box h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-top: 16px; }
  .site-box ul { margin: 14px 0 0; padding-left: 1.1em; display: grid; gap: 10px; color: var(--text-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .privacy { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } .site-box { position: static; } }
</style>
